    "title": "Different Ways to Add Parentheses",
    "workload": "build 6 token vectors once from 11-operator expressions with differing operator cycles, then 30 punches of the full Catalan-exponential divide-and-conquer (4862 -> 58786 parenthesizations per call), deliberately UNMEMOIZED as in the kata so every operator split recomputes both sub-spans. Sink is the sum of every value produced, which is order-independent so all five agree regardless of recursion push order. NOTE: every lane heap-allocates a fresh result vector per recursive call; C uses malloc/realloc rather than a shared scratch arena so the allocation behaviour matches.",
